{"duration_api_ms":231082,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a4fb9cb4-4ca0-46f0-beda-15e462b63ba8","total_cost_usd":0.277148,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13086,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22480,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15982},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13086,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":22480,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13086},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":22480,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13086,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.277148,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":15982,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Every feasible point sits at large D (about 3.2-3.3 m), high bluntness (1.1-1.18), cone angle near 70 deg and gamma between -2.2 and -3.5 deg. The hypervolume is 0.331. In normalised terms, 1 K of bondline temperature is worth about 0.6% of hypervolume, while 10k W/m2 of flux is worth only about 0.15%. Lowering bondline temperature therefore matters most. Two constraints bound the corner. max_g caps gamma at about -3.6 deg (limit about 12 g, roughly 1.6 g per degree, almost independent of D, bluntness and cone). The heatshield mass fraction caps D. Its margin scales roughly with D^2, and my extrapolation puts the limit near D = 3.38-3.40 m. The unexplored gains are a larger D, bluntness up to 1.35, and a spread of gamma values along the front.\",\"evidence\":[\"D sweep at gamma -3.4 and bluntness 1.1: C-897b67e590d7 (D 2.9) gives 344k W/m2 and 403.0 K, C-5e1c13074d20 (D 3.2) gives 298.7k and 396.9 K, and C-84c7c9af373d (D 3.3) gives 285.8k and 395.0 K. Larger D lowers both objectives.\",\"Mass-fraction margin versus D: 0.263 at 2.9 m (C-897b67e590d7), 0.103 at 3.2 (C-5e1c13074d20), 0.0748 at 3.25 (C-26ce9aa66580), 0.0455 at 3.3 (C-84c7c9af373d). The margin follows a D^2 scaling and would reach zero near 3.38 m. Bluntness 1.18 with cone 70 adds about +0.003 (C-15f0016ca61b, C-51e48573fc56).\",\"Gamma sweep at D 3.2, bluntness 1.1, cone 69: gamma -3.25, -3.4, -3.55 and -3.7 give g 11.40, 11.64, 11.89 and 12.14, and bondline temperature 398.5, 396.9, 395.3 and 393.8 K. C-114b79b08144 (gamma -3.7) violates max_g at 12.136 g.\",\"g depends almost only on gamma. C-7e930f570744 (gamma -4.54) gives 13.57 g and C-0a0993b4b67b (gamma -7.07) gives 18.8 g, while D and bluntness change g by only about 0.4 g per metre. Steeper entry cannot be bought back through geometry.\",\"Bluntness 1.0 (cone 66), 1.1 (cone 69) and 1.18 (cone 70) at D 3.2, gamma -3.4 give 305.1k, 298.7k and 294.4k W/m2 and 397.7, 396.9 and 396.3 K (C-b6ef7565262e, C-5e1c13074d20, C-15f0016ca61b). Higher bluntness helps both objectives, and the mass margin does not degrade.\",\"Shallow-gamma front points C-b86d67fded52 (gamma -2.2: 263.6k, 411.2 K) and C-a2a24d2b0ad2 (gamma -2.6: 277.6k, 406.3 K) show the flux versus temperature trade-off. A larger D and higher bluntness should shift this curve down and left.\",\"All 8 geometry failures have a small cone angle relative to bluntness. From the reported negative cone lengths I fit a rough overlap condition, cos(theta)*(about 1.86*b - 0.1) < 0.9. Cone 70 with b up to 1.35 gives about 0.82-0.85, so it should be buildable. Cone 69 with b 1.3 gives about 0.83-0.86, also inside the limit. C-15f0016ca61b (b 1.18, cone 70) and C-51e48573fc56 already built.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating falls with nose radius and with lower ballistic coefficient (larger D and bluntness). Peak bondline temperature follows the heat load, which is lower for a shorter, steeper pulse. Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, since g_max is roughly independent of ballistic coefficient. The best corner is therefore the largest D the mass fraction allows (about 3.36-3.38 m), the largest bluntness the geometry allows (1.35 at cone 70), and gamma near the g limit (about -3.5 to -3.55 deg). Sweeping gamma from -1.8 to -3.4 at that D and bluntness fills the flux versus temperature front with points below the current one.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The extrapolation to b 1.35 is outside the sampled range, and the effect of bluntness on mass fraction there is unknown. The mass-fraction edge near D 3.38 is uncertain by about ±0.01 in margin. The g margin at gamma -3.55 is only about 0.5-1%. The geometry-overlap fit uses only 8 failures and could be wrong near b 1.35. I extrapolated the flux D-exponent of about -1.35 from a few points. All predicted values come from local linear extrapolation of the data shown, not from a validated model.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Main corner candidate: D up to 3.36, b 1.35, cone 70, gamma -3.5 gives the lowest expected temperature while keeping g and mass margins.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether larger D and b 1.35 dominate the current front (about 285.8k, 395 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"Same corner at gamma -3.4, which has more g margin (about 2.5%) than gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":267000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A safer-g point on the front, and it separates the effect of gamma from D and b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma toward the g limit to minimise temperature at D 3.36.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g edge, with predicted g about 11.94 against a limit of 12.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the mass-fraction edge at D 3.38, where predicted margin is about 0.01, to find how much larger D can go.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":267400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D limit set by mass fraction and shows whether the D gain continues.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D of 3.30 with b 1.35 and gamma -3.55 gives a comfortable mass margin (about 5%) and still lowers temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the effect of b 1.35 at a D already known to be feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness sensitivity: b 1.25 at D 3.36, gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Together with the b 1.35 and b 1.30 points it maps the bluntness trend.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-15f0016ca61b\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at moderate gamma -3.0 with the large-D, high-b design.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between about 262k and 249k W/m2 with a well-margined design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a2a24d2b0ad2\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at gamma -2.6, improving on the existing point (277.6k, 406.3 K).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-a2a24d2b0ad2 in both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow entry (gamma -2.2) at large D and b 1.35 targets the low-flux end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-b86d67fded52 (263.6k, 411.2 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b86d67fded52\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the low-flux end of the front to gamma -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks extrapolation to shallow gamma, which is beyond sampled data for this D and b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at gamma -3.4 gives a safer g margin while probing the mass edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Distinguishes mass-fraction failure from g failure at D 3.38.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-26ce9aa66580\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.34 at gamma -3.45 is a moderate-risk corner point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the D and gamma grid between the D 3.30 and 3.36 points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.32 at gamma -3.5 keeps about 3.5% mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.32,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps D dependence of both objectives at fixed gamma and b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-51e48573fc56\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness sensitivity at b 1.30.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the bluntness benefit is linear up to 1.35.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5b1ddf3a40e9\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at gamma -3.2 with the large-D, high-b design.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a well-margined point (g about 11.4) between the low-flux end and the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a2a24d2b0ad2\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at gamma -2.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":252000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between the -2.6 and -3.0 points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a2a24d2b0ad2\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at gamma -2.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between the -2.2 and -2.6 points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-26ce9aa66580\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.34 at gamma -3.55 is a lower-D alternative to the D 3.36 gamma -3.55 point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the g edge with a slightly smaller D, which gives lower g and a larger mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1725b5526d3f\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly lower cone angle (69) at b 1.30 tests how cone affects the objectives and whether the geometry constraint is loose enough.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the geometry-overlap fit for b 1.3 at cone 69 (predicted overlap term about 0.83-0.86, limit 0.9) and the cone effect on flux and temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-84c7c9af373d\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.37 at gamma -3.5 refines the mass-fraction edge between 3.36 and 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Together with the D 3.36 and 3.38 points it brackets the mass-fraction limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":180357,"type":"result","duration_ms":231131,"uuid":"da0da4c4-afa9-4606-939e-c155de50423d","ttft_stream_ms":1229,"time_to_request_ms":49,"first_content_frame_ms":1229,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
